  "conclusion": "MODEL ESTIMATE: figures below come from an analytical model with stated assumptions, validated only where noted; they are not measurements. All 6 variants reproduce the reference on every simulated nonce (mismatches: 0); full pipelines accept one nonce per cycle. Midstate pipeline: 128 stages, 1201 adders, 93696 register bits; with precompute + early reject + constant folding: 122 stages, 1062 adders (11.6% fewer), 81824 register bits (12.7% fewer). Constant folding applied to a design without midstate removes block 1 and the first three second-block rounds automatically, giving exactly the midstate + precompute datapath. Best modelled FPGA: midstate+precompute3+early-reject+fold on Xilinx Virtex UltraScale+ XCVU9P at up to 6.80 GH/s (model). Measured CPU baseline 115.8 MH/s; model/CPU throughput ratio up to 59x. Measured GPU baseline 498.8 MH/s; model/GPU throughput ratio up to 13.6x. Energy figures depend on assumed per-toggle energies; treat them as order-of-magnitude until calibrated with vendor power tools or board measurements.",
